All,

The 4" Tapped Tees, also referred to as Service Tees, found in our C900 Pro=
duct Line differ in form from that of the 6" and 8".  These are the three s=
izes of this configuration found in the product line.  These fittings are p=
ressure rated complying with AWWA C907, the industry standard for molded PV=
C pressure rated fittings for use with Cast Iron Outside Diameter (CIOD) PV=
C pipe complying with AWWA C900.

See the first three attachments with file names indicating diameter depicti=
ng the form of the three sizes.

The 4" has a short branch of relatively large diameter that is constant in =
diameter as the female threaded outlet changes in size.  This branch has th=
ick walls.  The branch of the 4" is more accurately termed a boss due to it=
s short length.  This boss provides the necessary reinforcement.  The 6" an=
d 8" have extended branches that vary in diameter with the diameter of the =
female threaded outlet and is relatively thin with constant thickness.  In =
the 6" and 8" the reinforcement is provided for on the inside of the fittin=
g.  See the fourth and fifth attachments.

The design of the 4" provides the performance required to pass the pressure=
 rating requirements of AWWA C907.  This external reinforcement design, reg=
ardless of boss diameter, does not deliver the performance required in the =
6" and 8" fittings.  The internal reinforcement and extended branch provide=
s the necessary performance in the 6" and 8" for compliance with AWWA C907.=
  The extended branch required in the larger diameters necessitates a thinn=
er branch to control the geometry and performance of the threads.

j

